  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize the Lowball half first. A solid A-2-3-4-5 low will almost always guarantee you a 4-card Badugi attempt. It is much easier to scoop with a strong low.\n\nDraw heavy early. If you don't have three cards to a good low or Badugi, discard all five cards in the first round. Don't fall in love with a King-high Badugi.\n\nSnowing: A bluffing technique where you stand pat (draw zero cards) as if you have a perfect hand, forcing opponents to fold their drawing hands even if you actually have nothing.",
    Player: "Prioritize the Lowball half first. A solid A-2-3-4-5 low will almost always guarantee you a 4-card Badugi attempt. It is much easier to scoop with a strong low.\n\nDraw heavy early. If you don't have three cards to a good low or Badugi, discard all five cards in the first round. Don't fall in love with a King-high Badugi.\n\nSnowing: A bluffing technique where you stand pat (draw zero cards) as if you have a perfect hand, forcing opponents to fold their drawing hands even if you actually have nothing.",
